course: dictionary
lesson: 4947
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Imprinting is one of them. «Ducklings follow the first moving thing they see after hatching; this is called imprinting.» Here the words about ducklings and their mother show that imprinting is a science word about how baby animals learn to follow.
explain: Now read this: «The shop used imprinting to put a logo onto 200 mugs.» There are no animals here, and a logo is a design. So imprinting means pressing a mark or design onto something. Ask yourself: what are the clues around the word?
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «a baby animal learning to follow» make sense in the mug sentence? No. Does «pressing a design onto something» make sense in the duckling sentence? No. The right meaning is the one that fits both the sentence and its clues.
fact: Imprinting has two meanings: a baby animal learning to follow and trust something, and pressing a mark or design onto something.
fact: «Ducklings follow the first moving thing they see after hatching, usually their mother.»
fact: Ducklings have «imprinted on» people, dogs and even boots, so the first thing they see does not always have to be their mother.
fact: The scientist Konrad Lorenz studied imprinting with geese.
fact: In design, imprinting means printing a logo or design onto things like T-shirts and mugs.
exercise: «Ducklings follow the first moving thing they see after hatching; this is called imprinting.» In this sentence, imprinting means: | Sleeping in a nest | Printing a logo onto a T-shirt | Hatching from an egg | *A baby animal learning to follow and trust the first thing it sees
exercise: A designer uses imprinting to put a logo on mugs. What does imprinting mean here? | Swimming in a pond | *Pressing a mark or design onto something | Waking up early | Learning to follow a mother duck
exercise: Find the word that means coming out of an egg: «...the first moving thing they see after hatching...» | usually | moving | *hatching | follow
test: Ducklings have «imprinted on» boots. What does that mean? | They were scared of boots | They printed a picture of boots | *They learned to follow boots as if boots were their mother | They ate the boots
test: Why might a scientist study imprinting with geese? | *To learn how baby birds learn to follow the first thing they see | To find out how fast geese can swim | To teach geese to hatch from eggs | To print logos onto geese
exam: Read: «The company used imprinting to decorate 500 mugs.» Which meaning fits best? | *Pressing a design onto something | Hatching from an egg | Swimming in a pond | A baby animal following its mother
